      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1886, Nortonville became one of only nine L&N towns to have a steam hoist for unloading freight, a rare feature at the time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nortonville%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A shaft coal mine opened in 1902 by the Nortonville Coal Company, boosting growth and leading to an electric power plant in the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nortonville%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s City Hall sits in a 1930s WPA-built high school, reflecting New Deal investment in local infrastructure.",
